{title: Be Thou My Vision}
{artist: Irish, 8th century, tr. Mary E. Byrne, 1905, versified by Eleanor H. Hull, 1912}
{key: D}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 72}
{copyright: Words: public domain. Chords © 2026 Simon Davy.}

{comment: Verse 1}
[D]Be Thou my [G]Vision, O [D]Lord of my [A]heart;
[D]Naught be all [G]else to me, [D]save that Thou [A]art;
[Bm]Thou my best [G]Thought, by [D]day or by [A]night,
[D]Waking or [G]sleeping, Thy [A]presence my [D]light.

{comment: Verse 2}
[D]Be Thou my [G]Wisdom, and [D]Thou my true [A]Word;
[D]I ever with [G]Thee and Thou [D]with me, [A]Lord;
[Bm]Thou my great [G]Father, I [D]Thy true [A]son;
[D]Thou in me [G]dwelling, and [A]I with Thee [D]one.

{comment: Verse 3}
[D]Be Thou my [G]battle Shield, [D]Sword for the [A]fight;
[D]Be Thou my [G]Dignity, [D]Thou my De[A]light;
[Bm]Thou my soul's [G]Shelter, Thou [D]my high [A]Tower:
[D]Raise Thou me [G]heavenward, O [A]Power of my [D]power.

{comment: Verse 4}
[D]Riches I [G]heed not, nor [D]man's empty [A]praise,
[D]Thou mine In[G]heritance, [D]now and al[A]ways:
[Bm]Thou and Thou [G]only, first [D]in my [A]heart,
[D]High King of [G]Heaven, my [A]Treasure Thou [D]art.

{comment: Verse 5}
[D]High King of [G]Heaven, my [D]victory [A]won,
[D]May I reach [G]Heaven's joys, O [D]bright Heaven's [A]Sun!
[Bm]Heart of my [G]own heart, what[D]ever be[A]fall,
[D]Still be my [G]Vision, O [A]Ruler of [D]all.
